    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_09c2410370b9eb606e18facedace0d50633a3ab7d23e0c7115e8c1f9de542d65",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Within the source's postulated model, an ultraviolet CPT-gauging premise is realized not as the rejected global point identification but as a canonical state-level boundary on invariant Planckian hyperbolae. Fourier scattering preserves the even/odd decomposition, and the corresponding zeta or beta functional equation turns boundary compatibility over the whole locus into the proposed zero condition.",
