    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_5e2a2d18af05df26b7fe5ce1c4c304039639073a35c78ad215ffb436ef4a14cf",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Reflection parity begins as the twofold-degenerate decomposition of dilation eigenfunctions and as their character under weighted inversion. Fourier scattering acts separately on those sectors with different gamma multipliers; in the subsequent boundary matching, the even multiplier is paired with the zeta functional equation and the odd sign and multiplier with the Dirichlet beta functional equation, producing distinct energy sets and breaking the initial parity degeneracy.",
