    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_e7c834f869e22209471788a9c4dda8fb7053a45e884190557445d08c763b3109",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source leaves the physical spectral dictionary deliberately non-unique: nontrivial zeros on the critical line are proposed as real-energy levels, analytically continued trivial zeros are read as imaginary-energy scattering resonances, and the same zero relations may instead mark missing absorption lines in a continuum. A trace-formula/density comparison is proposed to distinguish absorption from emission, while entropy, multiparticle, and lower-bound questions test the broader adequacy of the construction.",
